 "result": "The failing call is in `src/tessel/sessions.py`, in `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`. The traceback points at **line 374**, `response.set_cookie(`, and the rejected argument is `partitioned=partitioned`, passed at line 382.\n\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie(          # sessions.py:374\n    name,\n    val,\n    expires=expires,\n    httponly=httponly,\n    domain=domain,\n    path=path,\n    secure=secure,\n    partitioned=partitioned,  # sessions.py:382, rejected by Werkzeug 3.0.3\n    samesite=samesite,\n)\n```\n\nWerkzeug 3.0.3 raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nThe same keyword is also passed to `response.delete_cookie(...)` at line 361, in the branch that clears an empty modified session. No test failed there, so the traceback doesn't confirm it, but Werkzeug 3.0.3 would reject it for the same reason.\n\nThe value comes from `self.get_cookie_partitioned(app)`, defined at `sessions.py:215` and read at line 344.",
